** Networking

Trust the local OpenSSL cert bundle for TLS connections (e.g. package
downloads) when it exists at this path.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(with-eval-after-load 'gnutls
  (add-to-list 'gnutls-trustfiles "/usr/local/etc/openssl/cert.pem"))
#+end_src

* Custom Keybindings

~C-c r~ reloads the configuration without restarting Emacs. Since
~user-init-file~ is ~init.el~, this re-tangles and re-loads
~config.org~ as well.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(global-set-key (kbd "C-c r") (lambda () (interactive) (load-file user-init-file)))
#+end_src

* Discoverability

** Which-Key

Pops up a list of possible continuations (and what they run) a
short moment after you press a prefix key like ~C-x~ or ~M-g~. Handy
for this config specifically since it now defines several
non-default prefixes and single-key overrides.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package which-key
  :init
  (which-key-mode)
  :custom
  (which-key-idle-delay 0.5))
#+end_src

* Completion

Vertico + Orderless + Marginalia: a minimal, composable completion UI
for the built-in minibuffer, as opposed to an all-in-one framework
like Helm or Ivy.

** Minibuffer Defaults

Tweaks to Emacs's own minibuffer behavior that pair well with
Vertico.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package emacs
  :ensure nil
  :custom
  ;; Enable context menu. `vertico-multiform-mode' adds a menu in the
  ;; minibuffer to switch display modes.
  (context-menu-mode t)
  ;; Support opening new minibuffers from inside existing minibuffers.
  (enable-recursive-minibuffers t)
  ;; Hide commands in M-x which do not work in the current mode. Vertico
  ;; commands are hidden in normal buffers. This setting is useful beyond
  ;; Vertico.
  (read-extended-command-predicate #'command-completion-default-include-p)
  ;; Do not allow the cursor in the minibuffer prompt.
  (minibuffer-prompt-properties
   '(read-only t cursor-intangible t face minibuffer-prompt)))
#+end_src

** Consult

Enhanced, Vertico-aware replacements for several built-in commands:
they add live preview and richer sources on top of what's already
there. ~C-x b~ now runs ~consult-buffer~ instead of plain
~switch-to-buffer~ (also lists recent files and bookmarks), ~M-g g~
upgrades ~goto-line~, and ~M-g i~ upgrades ~imenu~, all keeping their
original default keys. ~M-s l~ searches the current buffer
(~consult-line~, like Vim's ~/~) and ~M-s r~ greps the project with
ripgrep (~consult-ripgrep~).

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package consult
  :bind
  (("C-x b" . consult-buffer)
   ("M-g g" . consult-goto-line)
   ("M-g i" . consult-imenu)
   ("M-s l" . consult-line)
   ("M-s r" . consult-ripgrep)))
#+end_src

** Embark

Contextual actions on whatever is at point or under the minibuffer
cursor — e.g. from a ~consult-buffer~ candidate, kill/rename it
without switching to it first. ~embark-consult~ adds live preview to
Embark's own collect buffers, mirroring what Consult already does
elsewhere.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package embark
  :bind
  (("C-." . embark-act)
   ("C-," . embark-dwim)
   ("C-h B" . embark-bindings))
  :init
  (setq prefix-help-command #'embark-prefix-help-command))

(use-package embark-consult
  :after (embark consult)
  :hook
  (embark-collect-mode . consult-preview-at-point-mode))
#+end_src

** Marginalia

Rich annotations (keybindings, docstrings, file info, ...) next to
minibuffer completion candidates.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package marginalia
  ;; Bind `marginalia-cycle' locally in the minibuffer. To make the binding
  ;; available in the *Completions* buffer, add it to the
  ;; `completion-list-mode-map'.
  :bind (:map minibuffer-local-map
         ("M-A" . marginalia-cycle))

  ;; The :init section is always executed.
  :init
  (setq marginalia-field-width 120)

  ;; Marginalia must be activated in the :init section of use-package such
  ;; that the mode gets enabled right away. Note that this forces loading
  ;; the package.
  (marginalia-mode))
#+end_src

** Orderless

Flexible, space-separated (out-of-order) completion matching style.

#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(use-package orderless
  :custom
  ;; Configure a custom style dispatcher (see the Consult wiki)
  ;; (orderless-style-dispatchers '(+orderless-consult-dispatch orderless-affix-dispatch))
  ;; (orderless-component-separator #'orderless-escapable-split-on-space)
  (completion-styles '(orderless basic))
  (completion-category-overrides '((file (styles partial-completion))))
  ;; Disable defaults, use our settings.
  (completion-category-defaults nil)
  ;; Emacs 31: partial-completion behaves like substring.
  (completion-pcm-leading-wildcard t))
#+end_src

